WEBVTT

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:01.680
Play!

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:03.900
<i>Oh, fine then.</i>

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:07.900
<i>My arm's warmed up now,
so why don't I give you a taste?</i>

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:09.360
<i>Of my...</i>

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:14.160
<i>...miracle Mario-balls!</i>

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:15.910
<i>A fastball!</i>

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:22.120
<i>No, it's not!</i>

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:05.930
<b>A Storm Brewing</b>

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:12.000
Strike!

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:13.190
You're out!

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:15.690
Fuurin

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:15.690
Fuurin

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:15.690
Tsujidou

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:15.690
Tsujidou

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:20.330
<i>It looks like we won't get any
more runs against that pitcher,</i>

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:23.210
<i>but we've gone two innings
without them scoring.</i>

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:29.710
<i>Right now, it's 14-0, so if I limit them
to four runs max in the next two innings,</i>

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:31.750
<i>the game gets called in our favor.</i>

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:37.010
Out!

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:38.230
<i>All right!</i>

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:40.600
<i>Just five more outs and the game gets called!</i>

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:42.970
<i>If we take this nice and steady, we can win!</i>

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:46.440
<i>Batting eighth, shortstop, Hagiwara-kun.</i>

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:49.460
What are you all playing at?!

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:52.790
If we don't score five runs in the next
two innings, the game will be called!

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:56.150
<i></i>You're<i> the one who gave them
that crazy handicap.</i>

00:02:59.220 --> 00:02:59.990
Right field!

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:03.130
All right!

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:04.660
That's two outs!

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:09.540
<i>Batting ninth, pitcher, Kunitomo-kun.</i>

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:10.830
I'm sorry about this.

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:16.300
Sure, he didn't know you, 
but even so, it was rude of Coach

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:20.510
to give a ten-run lead to a team
that plays the game right.

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:22.210
Oh, uh, it's fine...

00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:26.930
But given how many girls are on your team,
it's sorta understandable...

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:32.080
Problem is, the team you're
walking all over right now

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:36.590
is mostly made up of backup players
and first-years. It's our B-Team.

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:40.700
Whoa!

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:42.660
Hell yeah!

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:45.820
Look at that!

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:47.580
Keep us rolling, scrubs!

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:50.270
<i>Mostly backup players and first-years?</i>

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:53.540
<i>We haven't been playing their starters?</i>

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:00.550
<i>A bunt?</i>

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:02.470
Third!

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:04.180
Wait, don't!

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:05.180
You won't make it!

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:06.570
Safe!

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:10.100
<i>Damn, if she'd thrown it,
I coulda bolted for home.</i>

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:12.080
Runners on first and third!

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:15.690
We're leading by 14 runs,
so does it really matter?

00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:19.570
<i>Thanks to Mario,
we're finally getting somewhere.</i>

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:24.150
<i>Even as the B-Team, they're useless if they
can't crush a pitcher like her the second time.</i>

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.210
Left!

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:29.870
Great! Just what I was going for!

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:38.640
Lucky!

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:39.880
That's one run back!

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:43.840
Um, you could've caught that, you know, Chiyo.

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:46.300
I-I'm sorry.

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:51.220
<i>Batting third, catcher, Inoue-kun.</i>

00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:52.770
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:55.190
<i>We can't do anything about Chiyo's fielding...</i>

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:57.650
<i>But they're reading Mutsuko's pitches now.</i>

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:00.320
Okay, keep us rolling, Inoue!

00:05:04.630 --> 00:05:05.860
The head coach?

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:10.410
<i>The A-Team's game ended early,
so we're on our way back.</i>

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:13.290
<b>Coach</b>

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:13.290
<b>The A-Team's game ended early
so we're on our way back</b>

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:13.290
<b>We'll be there soon,
so vacate the field.</b>

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:13.290
<i>We'll be there soon, so vacate the field.</i>

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:15.250
Fuurin

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:15.250
Fuurin

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:15.250
Tsujidou

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:15.250
Tsujidou

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:18.210
Play!

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:23.170
<i>Daigo told me I could go all out
since I've got Nishina as backup.</i>

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:28.340
<i>But as the ace, I have to get 
through this game by myself!</i>

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:31.920
First!

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:34.640
Mutsuko!

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:39.730
No!

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:40.480
Safe!

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:41.940
Home!

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:45.280
Safe!

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:47.990
Fuurin

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:47.990
Fuurin

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:47.990
Tsujidou

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:47.990
Tsujidou

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:47.990
Yeah, that's two!

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:49.890
Don't worry about it.

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:51.720
I-I'm sorry.

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:56.360
<i>Anita's not used to being on first, 
so she made an error too. This is bad.</i>

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:57.000
Timeout!

00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:00.940
Can I speak to whoever's
in charge of your team?

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:10.260
Ah, sorry! I'm the captain. Will I do?

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:11.720
What's this?

00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:13.180
What's going on?

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:14.240
What?!

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:15.890
You want to end the game <i>now</i>?!

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:21.470
There's been a schedule change,
so we no longer have use of the field.

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:27.570
Well, we'll chalk this up as a win for
you guys, so you can head off now.

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:30.510
The game's over!

00:06:30.510 --> 00:06:33.240
The A-Team will be back any minute,
so prep the field for them!

00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:36.870
For real, Coach?

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:38.460
It was just getting good.

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:40.920
You guys took too long to get into gear!

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:45.130
Fuurin

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:45.130
Fuurin

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:45.130
Tsujidou

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:45.130
Tsujidou

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:42.420
Wipe that off!

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:45.130
If the head coach sees 
that score, I'll be in trouble!

00:06:45.410 --> 00:06:49.040
Pretty up the scorebook too!
Make it, uh, 14-10 or something.

00:06:49.690 --> 00:06:50.740
<i>Falsify the score?!</i>

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:52.430
Wait, hold on a minute.

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:56.680
If something came up and
the game has to end now, that's fine,

00:06:56.680 --> 00:07:00.440
but could you at least let us know when 
we can play our next practice game?

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:01.520
What?

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:05.360
It was agreed that we'd play
each other again if we won.

00:07:07.850 --> 00:07:10.680
<i>He's getting cocky because
they were in the lead.</i>

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:13.660
<i>Playing them again won't do us any good.</i>

00:07:14.610 --> 00:07:18.180
Yeah, sure, sounds fine.
Maybe next year in the spring or something.

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:19.080
Next <i>year</i>?!

00:07:19.590 --> 00:07:22.580
That ain't no way to treat our guests...

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:24.540
...Yoneyama.

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:28.510
B-Boss!

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:31.470
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:31.470
<b>Head
Coach</b>

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:31.470
<b>Kunitomo</b>

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:33.180
"B-Boss"?

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:34.680
He looks like a character.

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:35.570
Scary!

00:07:35.570 --> 00:07:39.390
Uh, like... an underworld boss?

00:07:42.950 --> 00:07:45.460
You been tamperin' with the scores, Yoneyama?

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:48.390
Why'd ya give 'em such
a big handicap to start with?

00:07:48.390 --> 00:07:50.160
W-Well, because...

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:51.620
Well, whatever.

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:54.070
Ending the game here ain't polite.

00:07:57.660 --> 00:08:03.030
I apologize to our guests from Fuurin for
pittin' ya against our B-Team of first-years.

00:08:03.030 --> 00:08:04.210
Starting now...

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:09.650
we'll treat ya right and field
our best players against you.

00:08:13.370 --> 00:08:16.060
We'll just pick up from
where you guys left off.

00:08:16.060 --> 00:08:17.100
That all right?

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:18.810
Y-Yes, sir.

00:08:18.990 --> 00:08:20.970
Hold up! Are you serious?

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:23.520
So, up to now, we've been
playing their backup players?

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:25.120
Looks like it.

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:28.390
That's why we managed to
keep pace with them before.

00:08:28.390 --> 00:08:29.580
Makes sense.

00:08:31.090 --> 00:08:32.540
Are you okay, Mutsuko?

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:36.780
We've still got a big lead. It's their A-Team,
but let's plow on and not worry about that.

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:37.640
Yeah.

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:43.130
Nishina, something wrong?

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:45.290
Oh, uh, no...

00:08:47.340 --> 00:08:48.970
<i>Is this for real?</i>

00:08:48.970 --> 00:08:52.210
<i>I'd been wondering where
he ended up after that.</i>

00:08:52.650 --> 00:08:56.160
It seems Coach Kunitomo, who was
due to take over in the near future,

00:08:56.660 --> 00:08:59.640
now won't be able to do so,
for various reasons.

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:07.270
<i>And now I find out... he's just
coaching at another middle school!</i>

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:13.690
<i>Batter change. Yoshii-kun
switches out for Ashley-kun.</i>

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:19.180
Huh? First, we get "Mario," an' now
there's another foreign name?

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:21.620
<i>Look who's talking.</i>

00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:24.580
So what is this now, the World Series?

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:28.040
Finally, a hot batter!

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:30.460
<i>So these are their starters.</i>

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:35.470
<i>This is the real Tsujidou,
the strongest team in the prefecture.</i>

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:38.690
<i>How good are they really?</i>

00:09:39.560 --> 00:09:40.480
Play!

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:45.640
Strike!

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:47.630
Huh. What d'you think?

00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:49.860
Not too bad, I guess.

00:09:50.140 --> 00:09:51.990
The girl on second is my type.

00:09:51.990 --> 00:09:53.160
Really?

00:09:53.740 --> 00:09:55.000
The shortstop's fine, too.

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:56.640
Okay, the center fielder for me.

00:09:56.640 --> 00:09:58.320
You can have the chick on third.

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:02.630
But you know, I'm not really a fan of this...

00:10:02.630 --> 00:10:05.790
Bullying these girls just ain't right.

00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:15.090
Nice! Three-run homer!

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:22.010
Fuurin

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:22.010
Fuurin

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:22.010
Tsujidou

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:22.010
Tsujidou

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:20.190
All right. At least the game 
can't be called next inning.

00:10:20.190 --> 00:10:22.010
Nice, Ash!

00:10:22.290 --> 00:10:24.000
Don't sweat it!

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:27.420
Our earlier errors cost us those runs.
Let's reset and do this!

00:10:28.650 --> 00:10:31.940
<i>Batting fifth, pinch hitter, Etou-kun.</i>

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:33.880
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:38.900
<i>He hadn't seen Mutsuko's low outside slider
before and still slugged it out of the park.</i>

00:10:44.950 --> 00:10:46.750
We're on a roll!

00:10:47.110 --> 00:10:48.710
Now they're only eight ahead.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:50.670
This is bad.

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:57.220
That's the A-Team for you! At this rate,
we'll make up those eight runs in no time.

00:10:57.710 --> 00:11:01.980
By the way, Boss, why'd you arrange
a practice game with these losers?

00:11:01.980 --> 00:11:04.620
It's been years since Fuurin had a strong team.

00:11:04.620 --> 00:11:09.100
There's a kid I coached before I came here
on their roster. I wondered how he was doin'.

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:10.970
A kid you coached?

00:11:13.590 --> 00:11:14.800
Ball four!

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:18.110
Hey, hey! The pitcher's shakin' like a leaf!

00:11:19.710 --> 00:11:22.780
<i>Batting seventh, pinch hitter, Kaji-kun.</i>

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:30.340
<i>It's no use. I can't contain them.</i>

00:11:30.340 --> 00:11:32.540
<i>These guys... hit differently!</i>

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:40.800
<i>Ouch!</i>

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:47.970
Mutsuko!

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:53.920
See, this is what I was talking about.

00:11:53.920 --> 00:11:58.230
It's dangerous for girls to play against boys.

00:11:59.930 --> 00:12:01.970
Mutsuko! Are you okay?

00:12:01.970 --> 00:12:03.070
Where did it hit you?

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:05.260
Mutsuko? Mutsuko!

00:12:16.260 --> 00:12:17.590
You all right?

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:20.060
It might be a rubber ball,
but it hit you dead on.

00:12:20.060 --> 00:12:22.860
Right on your pivot leg, too, 
so don't go pushin' yourself.

00:12:22.860 --> 00:12:24.720
I'm fine, thank you.

00:12:24.990 --> 00:12:26.440
Are you sure?

00:12:26.440 --> 00:12:29.630
It's only a practice game,
so shouldn't we play it safe?

00:12:29.630 --> 00:12:32.110
Why don't you just switch with Nishina?

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:35.140
I said I was fine, really.

00:12:35.140 --> 00:12:37.610
Come on, everyone, back to your places.

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:38.570
Mutsuko...

00:12:39.060 --> 00:12:40.160
I get it.

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:45.780
It's not just my ankle.
My pitches aren't good enough.

00:12:47.840 --> 00:12:50.760
But Nishina still has to warm up.

00:12:50.760 --> 00:12:52.830
We need one more out this inning.

00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:55.610
I'll get it for us.

00:12:57.080 --> 00:12:58.040
All right.

00:12:58.590 --> 00:13:00.100
She's carrying on?

00:13:00.100 --> 00:13:01.840
How tenacious.

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:04.550
Fuurin

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:04.550
Fuurin

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:04.550
Tsujidou

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:04.550
Tsujidou

00:13:02.100 --> 00:13:04.550
Looks like this is the inning we catch up.

00:13:07.070 --> 00:13:07.950
Ball!

00:13:14.050 --> 00:13:14.850
Ball!

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:16.880
Let him hit, let him hit!

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:22.780
<i>If only I'd caught that fly ball.
This inning would've been over.</i>

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:27.360
Hit by pitch!

00:13:28.300 --> 00:13:30.400
Yes, bases loaded!

00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:32.010
We're not done yet!

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:43.230
<i>I can't get that last out.</i>

00:13:43.230 --> 00:13:44.560
<i>This is so frustrating!</i>

00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:48.550
<i>Batting ninth, pitcher, Kunitomo-kun.</i>

00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:01.460
Nishina?

00:14:02.120 --> 00:14:04.760
Senpai, you can't keep going with that leg.

00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:06.050
I'll pitch.

00:14:14.900 --> 00:14:17.040
Our pitcher is switching
with our right fielder.

00:14:20.900 --> 00:14:22.860
I mean to say, <i>please</i> let me pitch.

00:14:23.970 --> 00:14:26.440
I'm super pissed off right now.

00:14:28.730 --> 00:14:30.760
Tsujidou's head coach over there

00:14:31.330 --> 00:14:34.590
is the same Kunitomo who was meant
to come to our school in the spring.

00:14:35.090 --> 00:14:36.570
What?!

00:14:38.300 --> 00:14:38.850
Play!

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:43.570
And that kid Mario is also a Kunitomo,
so he's probably his son.

00:14:44.070 --> 00:14:46.450
I don't know what his reasons were,

00:14:46.450 --> 00:14:52.030
but this guy betrayed us, then shamelessly
agreed to a practice game against us.

00:14:52.680 --> 00:14:54.990
I'm done with him playing us for fools.

00:14:55.890 --> 00:14:58.370
I can't just keep taking it
when he's gone this far!

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:03.780
Strike!

00:15:11.050 --> 00:15:13.470
<i>Nishina-kun, do your best!</i>

00:15:16.490 --> 00:15:17.800
Strike!

00:15:21.530 --> 00:15:23.040
This guy's fast.

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:25.230
Unlike that girl's pitches.

00:15:25.500 --> 00:15:27.150
<i>All right, we've cornered him.</i>

00:15:27.150 --> 00:15:29.690
<i>Let's tempt him with a pitch
outside the strike zone.</i>

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:33.830
<i>I'm not the person you knew a year ago.</i>

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:37.200
<i>I'll make you regret turning your back on me!</i>

00:15:39.880 --> 00:15:40.910
Left!

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:45.340
<i>Oh no! It's all over!</i>

00:15:46.970 --> 00:15:48.170
Chiyo!

00:15:48.170 --> 00:15:50.630
Get it!

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:57.310
No way!

00:15:57.490 --> 00:15:58.480
Yes!

00:15:58.480 --> 00:15:59.770
For real?

00:16:00.490 --> 00:16:01.480
Out!

00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:03.730
Three outs. Change sides!

00:16:07.380 --> 00:16:08.760
Nice catch!

00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:10.650
Good job, Chiyo!

00:16:11.250 --> 00:16:13.450
You saved us, Chiyo.

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:20.440
Limited to six runs, huh?

00:16:20.440 --> 00:16:22.500
I would've liked two or three more.

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:23.560
Yoneyama.

00:16:23.560 --> 00:16:24.490
Yes?

00:16:24.490 --> 00:16:27.040
Inoue will probably be fine,

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:29.470
but I can't get a feel for this team.

00:16:29.470 --> 00:16:31.670
Get Sakaguchi out here, just in case.

00:16:31.670 --> 00:16:33.340
He should be in the computer lab.

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:37.670
Strike!

00:16:38.510 --> 00:16:40.390
<i>We're still eight runs ahead,</i>

00:16:41.110 --> 00:16:45.150
<i>but if it wasn't for the handicap,
they would've overtaken us and it'd be 6-4 now.</i>

00:16:45.700 --> 00:16:49.880
<i>Mario's pitches are fast, and I don't 
even </i>know<i> what that breaking ball is.</i>

00:16:50.430 --> 00:16:53.950
<i>And their A-Team's batting 
skills are also next level.</i>

00:16:54.520 --> 00:16:56.560
<i>They're definitely not a team we can beat.</i>

00:16:57.240 --> 00:17:01.580
<i>I don't know how much of that is their
coach's doing in the last six months...</i>

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:09.290
Oh, right! Kan-chan's a southpaw killer!

00:17:12.750 --> 00:17:13.740
Out!

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:16.600
A right grounder?!

00:17:16.600 --> 00:17:18.180
Too slow!

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:21.140
<i>Batting ninth, left field, Fujii Chiyo-san.</i>

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:26.020
<i>But we're not going to give up!</i>

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:28.910
<i>Even if we need the handicap to do it,
a win means we play them again.</i>

00:17:28.910 --> 00:17:32.440
<i>And if we play strong teams, 
our team can get stronger, too!</i>

00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:35.780
Ball four!

00:17:36.180 --> 00:17:37.240
Time!

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:39.700
Stay there!

00:17:40.210 --> 00:17:42.000
I know already, so leave me alone!

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:44.040
I don't need your advice!

00:17:44.400 --> 00:17:47.370
<i>That clown. He's letting it get to him.</i>

00:17:47.370 --> 00:17:51.250
<i>He may have a big frame, but he's still
just a kid. That's my little brother for you.</i>

00:17:55.860 --> 00:17:56.550
Safe!

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:57.910
Nice!

00:17:57.910 --> 00:18:00.010
One out, runners on first and second!

00:18:00.520 --> 00:18:03.320
<i>Batting second, shortstop, Sagara-san.</i>

00:18:03.320 --> 00:18:05.350
That odd couple is doing well.

00:18:05.810 --> 00:18:07.940
Boss, should I warm up?

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:11.270
Mario's slipping into bad habits again.

00:18:12.540 --> 00:18:13.480
Ball!

00:18:14.010 --> 00:18:16.820
No. Sakaguchi's comin'. That should be enough.

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:19.450
He'll straighten him out.

00:18:19.450 --> 00:18:21.160
Room

00:18:21.470 --> 00:18:22.780
Hey, Sakaguchi.

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:24.440
The head coach asked for you.

00:18:24.440 --> 00:18:27.120
We might need you in this 
practice game, so get out here.

00:18:27.470 --> 00:18:29.500
Can I just have a minute more?

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:32.590
I'm almost done inputting
the data from our last game.

00:18:33.100 --> 00:18:34.300
Okay, but make it quick.

00:18:34.810 --> 00:18:36.000
I will.

00:18:49.160 --> 00:18:50.600
All right!

00:18:49.160 --> 00:18:50.600
Yes!

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:53.030
Mario! You gotta cover!

00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:58.400
Ya gotta laugh. Just a textbook
example of him workin' himself up.

00:19:00.100 --> 00:19:01.940
One out, bases loaded!

00:19:01.940 --> 00:19:03.620
Keep it up!

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:05.240
<i>I don't care anymore.</i>

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:09.080
<i>He refuses timeouts. He only throws 
fastballs. Go ahead and self-destruct.</i>

00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:10.990
Chill out, Mario!

00:19:11.290 --> 00:19:12.480
<i>Okay.</i>

00:19:12.480 --> 00:19:15.280
<i>Two more runs, and the mercy
rule comes into play again.</i>

00:19:15.280 --> 00:19:18.260
<i>As long as he doesn't throw his 
miracle ball, we can do this.</i>

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:20.440
Ball!

00:19:23.880 --> 00:19:24.870
Ball!

00:19:25.480 --> 00:19:28.560
Boss, he'll completely fall apart 
if you don't switch him out.

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:33.000
Don't you think it's too early to put Mario in
an A-Team uniform when he's still a first-year?

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:34.310
It's fine.

00:19:34.310 --> 00:19:36.780
No better time to bully him
than a practice game.

00:19:37.800 --> 00:19:42.240
You'd have a point if it was any other player,
but he's my son. I won't go easy on him.

00:19:42.240 --> 00:19:45.030
If he's gonna fall apart,
the sooner the better.

00:19:48.070 --> 00:19:49.200
She got it!

00:19:50.450 --> 00:19:51.360
Out!

00:19:53.010 --> 00:19:55.240
But it was good enough for a sacrifice fly!

00:19:55.670 --> 00:19:57.370
Chiyo's running!

00:19:57.370 --> 00:19:59.030
She didn't tag up?!

00:19:59.030 --> 00:19:59.630
Third!

00:20:00.310 --> 00:20:01.670
No!

00:20:02.120 --> 00:20:03.640
S-Safe!

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:05.600
That was close.

00:20:05.810 --> 00:20:09.070
Chiyo, did you forget 
how to play baseball?

00:20:09.070 --> 00:20:10.060
S-Sorry.

00:20:11.380 --> 00:20:13.470
<i>I thought that was outta here.</i>

00:20:15.100 --> 00:20:17.480
<i>She's a good hitter, that one.</i>

00:20:17.710 --> 00:20:21.030
<i>Batting fourth, catcher, Shigeno-kun.</i>

00:20:21.540 --> 00:20:23.450
<i>Wait a minute. Now I get it.</i>

00:20:24.460 --> 00:20:26.810
<i>The reason he isn't 
throwing those breaking balls</i>

00:20:26.810 --> 00:20:29.540
<i>is probably because the 
catcher can't catch them!</i>

00:20:30.600 --> 00:20:32.750
<i>Drop it a few more times
and we'd figure it out.</i>

00:20:32.950 --> 00:20:35.660
<i>With runners on base,
it's an even riskier option.</i>

00:20:38.300 --> 00:20:41.430
<i>If he just keeps throwing it
down the pipe, we're not scared!</i>

00:20:43.350 --> 00:20:44.130
Foul!

00:20:45.610 --> 00:20:48.550
Huh. He's got a nice swing.

00:20:49.090 --> 00:20:50.520
Oh, you're here.

00:20:50.960 --> 00:20:51.990
Timeout!

00:20:51.990 --> 00:20:53.460
Field change.

00:20:53.460 --> 00:20:55.980
Catcher Inoue switches with Sakaguchi.

00:20:56.790 --> 00:20:58.100
Changing the catcher?

00:20:58.700 --> 00:20:59.750
What?

00:20:59.750 --> 00:21:01.400
He's probably the starter.

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:04.860
I guess the catcher was
 the only one still in white.

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:10.740
Sakaguchi?

00:21:11.610 --> 00:21:13.090
Good work, Inocchi.

00:21:13.570 --> 00:21:15.290
Th-Thanks. Good luck.

00:21:25.270 --> 00:21:27.040
H-Hikaru?

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:31.430
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:31.430
<b>Sakaguchi Hikaru</b>

00:21:28.070 --> 00:21:29.220
It's been a long time.

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:31.430
You're looking well, Daigo-kun.

00:21:31.690 --> 00:21:32.560
Huh?

00:21:32.560 --> 00:21:34.390
What are you doing here, Hikaru?

00:21:34.630 --> 00:21:36.440
I thought that was him!

00:21:36.440 --> 00:21:37.410
You know him?

00:21:37.410 --> 00:21:38.420
Yeah!

00:21:38.420 --> 00:21:40.360
We played Little League together.

00:21:40.860 --> 00:21:42.880
But then he moved to Gunma.

00:21:43.480 --> 00:21:44.900
A lot's happened.

00:21:45.540 --> 00:21:47.780
I came back here in my
first year of middle school.

00:21:48.090 --> 00:21:49.490
I-I see.

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:52.820
But it's great to see you're all better now!

00:21:52.820 --> 00:21:56.730
I never would've guessed
you'd become a catcher.

00:21:57.970 --> 00:21:59.380
Yeah...

00:21:59.380 --> 00:22:02.220
I can't pitch anymore, you see.

00:22:02.740 --> 00:22:03.670
Because of that injury.

00:22:05.920 --> 00:22:08.910
Hey! Stop yakking and start playing already!

00:22:08.910 --> 00:22:10.820
Oh, sorry about that.

00:22:20.660 --> 00:22:23.720
<i>He can't pitch anymore...</i>

00:22:26.290 --> 00:22:27.680
<i>...because of that injury.</i>

00:24:00.920 --> 00:24:03.400
Hikaru-kun is at Tsujidou?!

00:24:03.400 --> 00:24:08.300
Hikaru-kun! We finally got
ourselves a real prince!

00:24:08.300 --> 00:24:10.210
Don't be so laid back.

00:24:10.580 --> 00:24:12.780
They're in a completely different league!

00:24:12.780 --> 00:24:16.410
This might be the only time 
everyone gets to play together.

00:24:16.410 --> 00:24:18.600
Huh? What do you mean, "the only time"?

00:24:18.600 --> 00:24:24.980
<b>Cinderella's Magic</b>

00:24:18.810 --> 00:24:21.280
Next time: "Cinderella's Magic."

00:24:21.280 --> 00:24:23.790
Run to the stage of your dreams!
